\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces CAP-KVC architecture. A background sweep evaluates candidate contexts from GPS, BLE, and time inputs, maintains up to three primed KV states across llama.cpp sequence slots, and persists each state to internal storage. When an interaction begins, Tier~1 immediately presents a canned response, then the engine resumes the highest-ranked resident slot to decode the user's intent. If no matching state is resident, background priming is scheduled (Tier~2). Slot~3 handles inline inference and benchmark executions without evicting resident states.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{3}{CAP-KVC architecture. A background sweep evaluates candidate contexts from GPS, BLE, and time inputs, maintains up to three primed KV states across llama.cpp sequence slots, and persists each state to internal storage. When an interaction begins, Tier~1 immediately presents a canned response, then the engine resumes the highest-ranked resident slot to decode the user's intent. If no matching state is resident, background priming is scheduled (Tier~2). Slot~3 handles inline inference and benchmark executions without evicting resident states}{figure.1}{}}
